    "['multipath [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 65008', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65008\\n neighbor RR peer-group\\n neighbor RR multipath multiple-as\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, you\\'ll need to first define the BGP process with the local AS number (which wasn\\'t explicitly shown in the Juniper config but would be needed in Cisco).\\n2. The peer-group \"RR\" would need to be created first (shown here for context).\\n3. The actual command translation is \"neighbor RR multipath multiple-as\" which enables multipath with multiple AS support for the RR peer-group, matching the Juniper functionality.', 'trans_template': 'router bgp 65008'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor RR peer-group', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65008\\n neighbor RR peer-group\\n neighbor RR multipath multiple-as\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, you\\'ll need to first define the BGP process with the local AS number (which wasn\\'t explicitly shown in the Juniper config but would be needed in Cisco).\\n2. The peer-group \"RR\" would need to be created first (shown here for context).\\n3. The actual command translation is \"neighbor RR multipath multiple-as\" which enables multipath with multiple AS support for the RR peer-group, matching the Juniper functionality.', 'trans_template': 'neighbor RR peer-group'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor RR multipath multiple-as', 'parent_command': ['router bgp [parameter1]', 'neighbor [parameter1] remote-as [parameter2]'], 'root': 'router bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 65008\\n neighbor RR peer-group\\n neighbor RR multipath multiple-as\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Cisco, you\\'ll need to first define the BGP process with the local AS number (which wasn\\'t explicitly shown in the Juniper config but would be needed in Cisco).\\n2. The peer-group \"RR\" would need to be created first (shown here for context).\\n3. The actual command translation is \"neighbor RR multipath multiple-as\" which enables multipath with multiple AS support for the RR peer-group, matching the Juniper functionality.', 'trans_template': 'neighbor RR multipath multiple-as'}]]": 1,
